# A store under a key that is one symbol as far as is seen lets its object escape. "As far as is seen" leaves out what came by escape alone, so a key of which nothing had been seen yet counted as a symbol:
# here `this` of fill() is known by escape alone at first (the constructor goes through a table under a name nobody knows), `-10 - node[i]` is a number by escape alone, and the first look at
# `empty[sub] = true` sent the local map out of sight for good. The next look said no; whether the first one came at all hung on the order of arrivals, and Link given more said more (FlowFindsLessFromMore).
# A key is a symbol as far as is seen only where a symbol has been seen. L1 = the map.
# RUN: link layouts mechanisms=all
# CHECK: layout L1 changes=[GainsProperty, ChangesPrototype] stays-with-compiled-code filled-under-computed-keys
# -- source: a-key-of-which-nothing-is-seen-yet-is-no-symbol.js
